        "title": {
          "en": "A short story"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Marks of five children were 4, 6, 6, 7, 10.\n\"What is a typical mark?\" asked the teacher."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "mean",
          "median",
          "mode"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "The mean is the sum divided by the number of values: 33 divided by 5 is 6.6. The mode is the most frequent value, which is 6. The median is the middle value when the data is in order, which is 6.\nThese three describe the data in different ways. The range is the biggest minus the smallest, which is 6.\nWe choose the measure that suits the data."
        }
